{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1510784-creation-megafauna-question","id":1510784,"title":"Creation Megafauna Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-05T07:04:33-07:00","id":1510784,"title":"Creation Megafauna Question","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">My posts on Ask a Question, Get an Answer 2 are all being blocked now by the extreme &quot;spam&quot; filter so I will never get to ask a Q there for months. So I am making a new thread. Exalted people, please help me.<br /> <br /> I have a question about<b></b>:<br /> Claw Ravagers<br /> and<br /> Thunder Lizards.<br /> <br /> Are they (described similar to) Spinosaurus and Brontosaurus?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Most importantly to me, where in Creation do they live? Direction, habitat, anything canon that you know would help me.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Halved-Ichor Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1435976-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-2?p=1509377#post1509377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iirc 3e core correctly, all these paleo-beasties are described using their in-universe names, with wording that doesn't reference irl knowledge on dinosaurs and extinct megafauna... and then you find an illustration of a T-Rex figthing a Triceratops next page.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1435976-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-2?p=1509449#post1509449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books, note won't probably ever say these explicitly. They're generally written around the idea of presetning things in-setting, so the equivalence of an animal to a real-world analog is something left for us to do. I have my own interpretation, including some stated by writers if not in text, here. Another list exists that I need to dig-up but does similarly. and I'll find that if need-be.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mtjlOB_YrEOSlF4cZbNCTZwRjp-EfPKpaMU03oSJX8k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Yes I understand, but I was hoping for just that kind of interpretation based on its description. I appreciate your list Blaque, although I disagree with you about river dragons (I prefer <i>Purussaurus</i>).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Maybe there are no swamp striders, but I know I saw a mention of claw ravagers at least once: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a> thinks they\u2019re <i>Spinosaurus</i>.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/238224-the-art-of-john-conway?p=240506#post240506</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Most of all I want to find out where in Creation (what Direction or more detail) claw ravagers, and also thunder lizards, live.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T07:13:34-07:00","id":1510787,"title":"","content":"The link/quote I attempted to post was this: <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/238224-the-art-of-john-conway?p=240506#post240506</span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only ex